*.mast linguist-language=Python
*.amd linguist-language=markdown

# The GitHub ARCHIVE (what `sbs.pyz fetch` downloads) leaves these out; a clone and the
# release workflow's `actions/checkout` still get everything, so the media pack is built
# from the real art as before. `export-ignore` only governs `git archive`.
#
# media/ travels as its own release asset instead - unpacked ONCE into `__lib__/media`
# and read from there, rather than copied into every mission that uses it. story.json
# declares it under `shared_media`, which resolves mission-local first, so a clone keeps
# editing art in place.
media/          export-ignore
mkdocs/         export-ignore
.github/        export-ignore

# The 34 ADDON folders travel as .mastlib release assets, the same way media/ does.
# A fetched copy therefore has no addon source and loads them from `__lib__` (they are
# declared in story.json); a CLONE still has every folder and MAST prefers the source,
# so editing an addon in place keeps working. Keep this list in step with
# __lib__.json - it is the single source of truth for what gets packaged.
#
# maps/ is deliberately NOT here: it is the mission's own content and is not packaged.
